      <fr:mainmatter>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://caimeo.space/def-0028/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>def-0028</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/def-0028/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Degree of polynomial">Degree of polynomial</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    A <fr:link href="/def-0027/" title="Polynomial" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-0027/" display-uri="def-0027" type="local">polynomial</fr:link> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[p\in  \mathcal {P}(R)]]></fr:tex> is said to have degree <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[n]]></fr:tex> if
    there exists coefficients <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[a_0, a_1, \ldots , a_n \in  R]]></fr:tex> and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[a_n \neq  0]]></fr:tex> such that
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        p(x) = a_0 + a_1 x + a_2 x^2 + \cdots  + a_n x^n
    ]]></fr:tex>
    for all <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x \in  R]]></fr:tex>. We denote the degree of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[p]]></fr:tex> by <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\deg (p) = n]]></fr:tex>.
    For the zero polynomial, we define its degree to be <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[-\infty ]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://caimeo.space/eg-0002/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>eg-0002</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/eg-0002/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Differentiation is linear map">Differentiation is linear map</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Example</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    Define <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D\in \mathcal {L}(\mathcal {P}(\mathbb {R}),\mathcal {P}(\mathbb {R}))]]></fr:tex> (recall that <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}]]></fr:tex> means <fr:link href="/def-0027/" title="Polynomial" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-0027/" display-uri="def-0027" type="local">set of polynomials</fr:link>) by
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        D(f) = f'
    ]]></fr:tex>
    We can see that <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D]]></fr:tex> a linear map.
    <html:ul><html:li>Additivity: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D(f+g) = (f+g)' = f' + g' = D(f) + D(g)]]></fr:tex></html:li>
        <html:li>Homogeneity: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[D(\alpha  f) = (\alpha  f)' = \alpha  f' = \alpha  D(f)]]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ul></html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://caimeo.space/def-0026/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>def-0026</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/def-0026/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="\mathcal {P}_m (R)">
              <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}_m (R)]]></fr:tex>
            </fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
    The set of all polynomials of degree at most <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[m]]></fr:tex> with coefficients in ring <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> is denoted by <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}_m (R)]]></fr:tex>.
    In other words,
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[
        \mathcal {P}_m (R) = \set { p \in  \mathcal {P}(R) | \deg (p) \leq  m}
    ]]></fr:tex>
    where <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {P}(R)]]></fr:tex> is the <fr:link href="/def-0027/" title="Polynomial" uri="https://caimeo.space/def-0027/" display-uri="def-0027" type="local">set of all polynomials</fr:link> with coefficients in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
